The ci directory houses helper files for the GitHub Actions workflows in $ROMS_ROOT/.github/workflows/

- compile_only.sh: compiles ROMS with a given set of CPP keys and no run; containerized_ci.yml uses it to check that CPP-key combinations the pytest suite doesn't run still compile (PARALLEL_IO with and without MPI_MASKING, DIAGNOSTICS, CDR forcing without MARBL)
- set_environs.sh: sets the ROMS environment variables for a conda environment (e.g. in a GitHub Codespaces session)
- pre-commit/: scripts for the repository's pre-commit hooks (.pre-commit-config.yaml)
- update_release_notes.py, finalize_release_notes.py, release_body.py: maintain docs/releases/ and the release text, run by the release-notes and publish workflows; test_*.py are their unit tests

The main workflows:
- containerized_ci.yml: builds the CI container images when they change and runs the pytest suite (tests/) in them, with gfortran and ifx
- pre-commit.yaml: runs pre-commit on every pull request and push to main
- sphinx.yaml: builds the documentation on every pull request
- automated_testing_workflow_python_mpc.yml: tests the mpc preprocessor (Tools-Roms/mpc_python) when it changes
